---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ContentSection from '../../components/ContentSection.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import LinkCard from '../../components/LinkCard.astro';

const relatedPages = [
  { title: 'NBA Betting Hub', href: '/nba-betting', description: 'Complete NBA guide' },
  { title: 'NBA Live Betting', href: '/nba/live-betting', description: 'In-game wagering' },
  { title: 'Load Management', href: '/nba/load-management', description: 'Rest effects' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="NBA Playoff Betting Guide"
  description="How NBA playoff betting differs from regular season, series dynamics, adjustment factors, and postseason market considerations."
>
  <Hero
    title="NBA Playoff Betting Guide"
    subtitle="Postseason Series Dynamics and Betting Considerations"
    size="medium"
  />

  <div class="container content-container">
    <article class="page-content">
      <ContentSection>
        <div class="quick-take">
          <h2>Quick Take</h2>
          <p>
            NBA playoffs feature seven-game series that allow for strategic adjustments and create different dynamics than single-game betting. Coaching adjustments, rotation tightening, and increased intensity change how teams perform. Markets are sharp due to concentrated attention, but understanding series dynamics and adjustment patterns can inform your analysis.
          </p>
        </div>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="How Do Playoffs Differ from Regular Season?" id="differences">
        <h3>Seven-game series create adjustment cycles</h3>
        <p>
          Teams adapt between games. A strategy that worked in Game 1 might be countered by Game 3. Coaching quality and preparation time become more important.
        </p>

        <h3>Rotations tighten significantly</h3>
        <p>
          Regular season 10-man rotations become 7-8 player rotations. Stars play more minutes. Depth matters less; top-end talent matters more.
        </p>

        <h3>Home court swings matter</h3>
        <p>
          NBA home court advantage is real. Series often follow predictable home/away patterns until the later games.
        </p>

        <h3>Motivation is maximized</h3>
        <p>
          No load management, no tanking considerations. Every team is trying to win every game.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="What This Means for Bettors" id="what-means">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Expect adjustments:</strong> Game 1 results don't predict series outcomes—both teams adapt.</li>
          <li><strong>Value home underdogs:</strong> Home court advantage is meaningful; road favorites can struggle.</li>
          <li><strong>Watch rotation changes:</strong> Who gets more or fewer minutes? Why?</li>
          <li><strong>Series price vs game price:</strong> Consider whether betting the series offers better value than individual games.</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Common Misconceptions" id="misconceptions">
        <h3>"Regular season record predicts playoff success"</h3>
        <p>
          Playoff basketball is different. Teams that coasted in the regular season often improve; teams that overperformed may regress.
        </p>

        <h3>"Sweeps are common"</h3>
        <p>
          Even heavy favorites rarely sweep. Underdogs typically steal at least one game.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Key Takeaways" id="takeaways">
        <ul>
          <li>Seven-game series allow for adjustments between games</li>
          <li>Rotations tighten; stars play more, depth matters less</li>
          <li>Home court advantage is significant</li>
          <li>Game 1 results don't predict series outcomes</li>
          <li>Consider series bets vs individual game bets</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Related Resources" id="related">
        <div class="related-grid">
          {relatedPages.map((page) => (
            <LinkCard title={page.title} href={page.href} description={page.description} />
          ))}
        </div>
      </ContentSection>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-content { padding: var(--spacing-3xl) 0; }
  .quick-take { background-color: var(--color-surface); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent); padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: 0 var(--border-radius) var(--border-radius) 0; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl); }
  .quick-take h2 { font-size: 1rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--color-accent); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); }
  .quick-take p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .related-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--spacing-md); margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .related-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
